## Vercel Web Analytics Integration

Successfully implemented Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js App Router project.

### Changes Made

**1. Installed Dependencies:**
   - Added `@vercel/analytics` package using npm
   - Updated package.json and package-lock.json

**2. Modified Files:**
   - **app/layout.tsx**: Added Analytics component to the root layout
     - Imported `Analytics` from '@vercel/analytics/next'
     - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after the WalletProvider and children components

### Implementation Details

This project uses the Next.js App Router pattern (app directory), so the Analytics component was integrated into the root layout file (app/layout.tsx). The component is placed at the end of the body tag to ensure it loads after the main content, following best practices for analytics integration.

The Analytics component will automatically track page views and Web Vitals metrics when the application is deployed to Vercel.

### Verification

✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ ESLint passed with no warnings or errors
✅ All dependencies installed correctly
✅ Lock file (package-lock.json) updated

### Files Modified
- `app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree

The implementation preserves all existing code structure and only adds the necessary changes for Web Analytics integration.
